############ 3d. THE WHOLE-SEQUENCE-SHAPE FIXTURES ############
CREATE SEQUENCE IF NOT EXISTS keeps a pre-existing sequence of ANY shape,
so the PRE-ADOPTION block is what decides whether 350 may adopt one --
it reads the catalogue row right after the CREATE and refuses on the
first attribute that is not this file's. The post-check at the end is
the SECOND gate, over what the file produced.
One fixture per attribute the file configures; each must be
REFUSED and the refusal must NAME that attribute. The last fixture is
the TWIN: a correctly shaped pre-existing sequence, which must be
ADOPTED -- without it every refusal above would also pass for a file
that refuses everything (#391).

