---- [seqstart] a catalogue row whose start is outside its own range ----
PostgreSQL's own DDL validates START against MINVALUE/MAXVALUE, so this
state cannot be reached with CREATE or ALTER SEQUENCE -- the fixture is
a direct catalogue UPDATE, because `pg_sequence` is what 350 READS and
a check is only worth having if it can be shown to fire (#342).
This arm is also WHY the shape block sits where it does: the round-5
draft asserted the shape in the post-check, and `ALTER SEQUENCE .. OWNED
BY` re-validates the whole sequence, so this state was refused there by
PostgreSQL -- `START value (5) cannot be greater than MAXVALUE (-1)`,
naming neither the file nor the repair -- and the arm was unreachable.
