############ 3e. NEW: THE SEQUENCE'S START IS THE CONFIGURED ONE ############
The round-5 check asked whether the start sits inside the sequence's
own range. EVERY LEGAL START DOES -- PostgreSQL's own DDL validates
that much -- so the only state it could ever refuse was the direct
catalogue UPDATE in 3d's [seqstart] arm. A sequence someone else
configured is in range by construction and was adopted.

The fixture is the one that matters in practice: a perfectly legal
sequence of this file's own type, increment, bounds and cycle, started
at MINVALUE + 1. It descends, it draws, and it is TWO numbers from
exhaustion -- after which every upload answers 503. 350 must refuse it
by name.
