---- [identity MUTANT] the same fixture, against a COPY of 350 without the identity check ----
The refusal above names the start, so it is the identity check's. In
round 6 this arm showed the file WITHOUT it adopting the fixture and
committing a sequence already exhausted. SINCE ROUND 7 THAT FIXTURE HAS
A SECOND, INDEPENDENT GATE: a fresh sequence's next value IS its start,
so block 1c's floor refuses the same fixture by its POSITION. The arm
below requires exactly that, and then shows the identity check is
still load-bearing on its own: a start that is not -1 but sits where the
floor admits it (-2) is refused by the real file and ADOPTED by this copy.
