---- [R8-X1] the bottom of the range: positions within two values of MINVALUE ----
Found in round 8 by this rehearsal's author and FIXED in round 8 (notes 19,
D-19.4). 1c summed the accounted value in bigint, and from a next value
at MINVALUE, or the one below the range that a sequence standing at
MINVALUE with is_called true reports, the sum left the bigint range: the
block stopped on PostgreSQL's unnamed `bigint out of range` before the
floor could name the refusal. 1c now declares the accounted value numeric
and takes the sum in numeric. Each of the three positions must be refused
BY THE FLOOR'S SENTENCE, naming the value the file would leave, before any
draw -- nothing commits, the position is unchanged. Then a COPY of 350
with the declaration put back to bigint, and one with the sum put back to
bigint, must each refuse all three UNNAMED: both lines are load-bearing.
